.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KIMAGE 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kimage
.Nd turn this machine into a cloud-init golden image, export its disk, and start virtual machines from it
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm build
.Nm
.Cm export
.Op Ar format Op Ar directory
.Nm
.Cm deploy
.Ar image count
.Nm
.Cm full
.Op Ar count
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
An older demonstration, from before golden images were built in virtual
machines: install kldload on a machine, make that machine the golden,
and start copies of it.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm build
Prepares
.Em this machine
to be copied: installs and enables cloud-init, deletes its SSH host keys,
empties its machine id and host name, clears the login records and
everything in
.Pa /tmp
and
.Pa /var/tmp ,
and snapshots the root dataset as
.Ql @golden .
.It Cm export Op Ar format Op Ar directory
Writes the root disk as qcow2, raw, VHD, VMDK or all four, to
.Pa /srv/images
by default.
.It Cm deploy Ar image count
Starts
.Ar count
machines named
.Ql kldload-node- Ns Ar n
from the image, each a copy of it in
.Pa /var/lib/libvirt/images
with its own host name through cloud-init.
A machine of that name whose disk is not that copy is left alone and the
command stops.
.It Cm full Op Ar count
All three.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev KIMAGE_DISK
The root disk; found by itself otherwise.
.It Ev KIMAGE_OUTDIR , Ev KIMAGE_NAME
Where and under what name to export; default
.Pa /srv/images
and
.Ql kldload-golden- Ns Ar YYYYMMDD .
.It Ev KIMAGE_RAM , Ev KIMAGE_CORES
Each machine's memory and processors; default 4096 MB and 4.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when done; 1 on a failure, named.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Not run for this page: see CAVEATS.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kimage full 3
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr klab 8 ,
.Xr kvm-clone 8 ,
.Xr kvm-create 8
.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-09-30, writing this page:
.Cm deploy
removed any machine named
.Ql kldload-node- Ns Ar n ,
with every disk it had.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
.Cm build
and
.Cm full
change the machine they run on: after them it has no SSH host keys, no
machine id and no host name until they are made again, and everyone's
temporary files are gone.
Run them only on a machine meant to become an image.
.Xr klab 8
and
.Xr kvm-clone 8
build goldens inside virtual machines and are the way to do this now.
